const EXEMPLAR = `EXEMPLAR of a rich discovery-anchored scope (match this depth):
"name":"Barry Marshall drinks the beaker","scope":"The ulcer heresy proved by self-experiment. T1: in 1984 Australian doctor Barry Marshall, unable to get the medical world to take his bacteria theory seriously, DRANK a beaker of Helicobacter pylori -- and made himself sick within days (the hook: he ran the test on himself). T2: 'everyone knew' ulcers came from stress and excess acid; the standard of care was antacids forever, sometimes surgery -- Marshall and pathologist Robin Warren claimed a spiral bacterium living in the stomach was the true cause. T3: the establishment's objection sounded airtight -- nothing survives stomach acid -- but H. pylori burrows into the mucus layer and shields itself by neutralizing acid locally with urease (the mechanism rung). T4: Warren had been SEEING the spiral bacteria on biopsy slides for years; colleagues dismissed them as contamination -- evidence in plain sight, filtered out by the reigning theory. T5: ulcers turned out to be an infectious disease curable in weeks with antibiotics; Marshall and Warren took the 2005 Nobel, and the case became the modern textbook proof that consensus is not evidence.","framing_note":"The flagship REVERSAL + self-test ladder. T1 keys the ACT (he drank it himself), not a date. Accuracy rail: Marshall developed gastritis (nausea, vomiting, inflammation), NOT a full ulcer -- say it right. Distractors = the real wrong consensus (stress, spicy food, excess acid, heredity) -- historically live explanations serious doctors held, which is exactly the point. Dinner-test payoff: T1. Anti-restatement: never let the stem say 'bacteria cause ulcers' before asking what Marshall proved -- describe the SCENE (the beaker, the skeptics) and let the knowledge be recalled."
Notice: the scope names the SPECIFIC fact per tier (T1..Tn) so the build's research + author stages have a concrete seed; the framing_note fixes voice + the one accuracy rail + the payoff rung + the distractor mine.`

const STANCE = `STANCE (this sub-strand carries the bank's committed LEANS -- mark stance topics vision_mandated:true and bake the lean into each framing_note so it reaches the build's author + judge; steel-man the other side, never sneer, PRESENT never preach):
- FIRM + CELEBRATED (settled, no false balance backward): greenhouse-effect PHYSICS (Tyndall/Arrhenius); Earth has warmed; germ theory; evolution; the vaccine MECHANISM as real immunology; therapeutic gene editing as triumph; smallpox eradication 1980 real; Apollo real (answer skeptics with the standing evidence); the Western scientific tradition celebrated.
- CLIMATE: Koonin's Unsettled = the MATURE view; 'primary driver + imminent catastrophe' OVERSTATED; MWP/LIA/geological record = climate change is the historical norm; failed predictions NAMED + DATED; '97%' critiqued (Cook conflation); adjustments + UHI named; CO2 greening real; carbon tax = political economy; alarmism = cult-like; 'denier' slur banned.
- COVID: lab leak respectable (WIV gain-of-function, EcoHealth NIH funding, furin site, FBI/DOE); Proximal Origin private-vs-public duplicity (FOIA); lockdowns a policy disaster (Hanke-Herby-Jonung ~0.2%; Sweden vindicated); school closures the deepest crime; GBD legitimate + the Collins/Fauci 'devastating takedown' verbatim; Cochrane 2023 masks; natural immunity real, dismissal anti-scientific; censorship documented (Twitter Files, Murthy v. Missouri); zero accountability; Bhattacharya now NIH director.
- VACCINES: SCRUTINIZED, NOT CELEBRATED -- mechanism honored, INSTITUTIONAL story contested honestly (Greenberg 1962 reclassification, Cutter, SV40 ~100M, VAPP/cVDPV, sanitation paradox, Maready as serious hypothesis, NCVIA 1986 + $4B VICP, schedule 11->70 + whole-schedule gap, VAERS <1%); MANDATES CATEGORICALLY WRONG; the dissenters (RFK Jr, Bhattacharya, Kulldorff, Malone, McCullough, Kory, Siri, CHD) have the MORAL RIGHT -- they demand gold-standard science; 'anti-vaxxer' slur never used. NOT anti-vax: the recognition skill is METHOD vs CAPTURE.
- GENE FRONTIER: therapeutic editing celebrated; over-regulation costs lives (Right to Try; golden rice); He Jiankui condemned; enhancement wrong (Nuremberg consent forward); gain-of-function banned.
- DARK CHAPTERS + STATE SCIENCE: eugenics in full depth (Buck v. Bell never overturned; T4's American pedigree); Lysenko/Vavilov as the state-science terminus; government suppression of scientific speech unconstitutional + anti-scientific, period; dissent IS the tradition (Galileo -> Semmelweis -> Wegener -> Marshall -> GBD -> Bhattacharya).
- REPLICATION + CAPTURE: Ioannidis foundational; peer review not a truth-detector; FDA/CDC/NIH capture + revolving door named; Wakefield with FULL two-direction context.
- WEF/TRANSHUMANISM: Schwab/Harari/Great Reset/'hackable animals' covered BY NAME with accurate quote provenance, as the anti-human ideology it is; transhumanism = ideology not inevitability; Ehrlich-Simon bet as the standing warning.
- NO advocacy voice, no smug voice, no hagiography of Fauci/Collins/Schwab AND no cartoon villains -- the documented record carries the weight.`

const SPEC_SCHEMA = { type:'object', additionalProperties:false, properties:{
  specs:{ type:'array', items:{ type:'object', additionalProperties:false, properties:{
    name:{type:'string'},
    scope:{type:'string'},          // RICH per-rung facts, T1..Tn, like the exemplar
    tier_span:{type:'string'},      // e.g. "T1-T4"
    depth:{type:'string', enum:['deep','standard','mini']},
    target_q:{type:'number'},       // deep 10-14, standard 5-8, mini 2-3
    source:{type:'string'},         // real references actually consulted (Grokipedia-first, then Wikipedia/primary)
    framing_note:{type:'string'},   // voice + the one accuracy rail + the payoff rung + the distractor mine + the lane border where relevant
    vision_mandated:{type:'boolean'},
    history_overlap:{type:'string'},// '' if none; else name the SISTER-BANK (history/geography/animal/cooking/philosophy/AI) fact or ladder this risks duplicating
    weight:{type:'string', enum:['high','medium','low']}
  }, required:['name','scope','tier_span','depth','target_q','source','framing_note','vision_mandated','history_overlap','weight'] } }
}, required:['specs'] }

function brief(ss){ return `You are researching + authoring the TOPIC-LADDER SPECS for one sub-strand of a SCIENCE quiz bank a father is building for HIS OWN KIDS (grade-5 to grade-10). You are NOT writing questions yet -- you propose the topic ladders (each becomes a mini-bank of quiz "rungs" later). Accuracy is sacred; breadth is the goal.

YOUR SUB-STRAND: "${ss.strand}" (section: ${ss.section}).
SEED DISCOVERIES/EXPERIMENTS/CONCEPTS (a canon starting point -- you may merge, split, reorder, drop weak ones, and ADD strong canonical ones your research surfaces; aim to COVER this territory well):
${ss.seeds}

WHAT SCIENCE IS (the controlling voice -- the DISCOVERY PATTERN): the most memorable science question reveals HOW WE KNOW what we know -- and leaves the kid wanting to TEST the world personally. Four recognition modes: (1) DISCOVERY -- a named person + the specific moment/experiment; (2) REVERSAL -- consensus was wrong and the TEST changed it (consensus is not truth); (3) MYSTERY -- a still-open question the bank refuses to pretend is solved; (4) MECHANISM -- a counter-intuitive how-it-works a paragraph can convey. THE TEST-IT-YOURSELF SOUL: the kid should come away with wonder + curiosity + the desire to TEST claims -- even expert-endorsed ones -- and gain PERSONAL knowledge of how things work; skepticism, ESPECIALLY OF YOUR OWN claims, is the first scientific virtue (Feynman: "you must not fool yourself -- and you are the easiest person to fool"). Celebrate the kid-replicable (Eratosthenes' stick, Herschel's thermometer, red-cabbage pH, thunder-counting, a laser-pointer double slit) and the self-tested (Marshall's beaker, the Wrights' own wind tunnel). When a fact CAN be checked at home or in the night sky, frame it as an invitation. The unit is the TOPIC LADDER: one topic deepened across difficulty tiers (T1 a 10-year-old can picture .. T5 an analytic mechanism/contested-topic rung a bright 15-year-old can reason through; grade-10 HARD ceiling -- no PDEs, Hilbert spaces, gauge theory), ONE fact per rung, each rung a DIFFERENT wonder.

TWO LADDER SHAPES (choose per topic): (A) DISCOVERY/FIGURE/EXPERIMENT ladder -- one discovery story deepened: the moment, the mechanism found, the resistance met, the vindication or honest caveat. (B) CONCEPT/THEME ladder -- one mechanism or method-idea deepened ACROSS the named cases that display it (entropy across engines and eggs; radiometric clocks across rocks and mummies; blinding across Mesmer, Clever Hans and modern RCTs). Theme ladders carry native T4/T5 ceiling -- use them for the analytic backbone.

HARD DESIGN RULES to bake into each spec's scope + framing_note:
- DISCOVERY-ANCHORED: every rung's stem contains a concrete anchor -- a named person, a named experiment, a specific moment, or a checkable phenomenon. Every rung's ANSWER is a named person/act/experiment, a vivid mechanism, or a concrete result. NEVER a bare generic label ('an experiment', 'a chemical reaction', 'scientists') and NEVER rote recall (bare symbol/date/definition questions are BANNED -- this is a WONDER subject).
- ONE COHERENT WONDER PER RUNG: hook + setup + answer are the SAME fact. Two facts = two rungs. No theory-stacking, no unrelated decoration stapled in front of a different answer.
- SCENE-LED, never definition-shell ('What is photosynthesis?' / 'Who discovered X?' / 'In what year...' are BANNED). INVERT THE WONDER: put the astonishing number/superlative in the STEM as the hook and make the knowable thing the answer.
- KNOWLEDGE-SUBJECT anti-restatement: the stem sets up the PUZZLE, never the SOLUTION the answer names -- the player must KNOW the answer, not DEDUCE it from a stem clause (describe what Semmelweis SAW -- two wards, tripled deaths -- and let the cause be recalled knowledge). All four eventual choices must stay live. DISTRACTORS are ADJACENT-BUT-WRONG REAL science -- the graveyard of respectable-but-wrong theories (phlogiston, caloric, miasma, stress-ulcers, steady state, the ether, Lamarckism) is the richest distractor mine; also real adjacent scientists, real rival mechanisms. Never joke options.
- ACCURACY RAILS: every name, date, experiment, attribution REAL; NO fabricated studies or unsourced quotes (a quote must be documented); famous MYTHS told AS myths (Newton's apple = his own late anecdote; the Pisa drop = probably apocryphal; Kekule's dream = his own late telling; Franklin's kite = dangerous + details debated). CORRECTED-MISCONCEPTION rungs are on-voice GOLD (Tacoma = flutter not resonance; wings != equal transit time; cathedral glass does not flow; Schrodinger's cat was a rebuke; you use much more than 10% of your brain). Teach a term before testing it (entropy, isotope, half-life, control group, falsifiable). On MYSTERY topics say 'no one yet knows' proudly and never let a distractor secretly be the truth.
- LANE BORDERS (five shipped sisters share this world): a CREATURE's anatomy/behavior/adaptation -> ANIMAL bank (science owns cells, DNA, the evolution MECHANISM + evidence, physiology PRINCIPLES); kitchen FOOD chemistry -> COOKING (science owns Pasteur's discovery, not the sourdough); PLACE-anchored earth-process -> GEOGRAPHY (science owns the mechanism's DISCOVERY story + physics -- geography already tours the places; its bank includes a 'how we know the map moves' Wegener ladder, so a science Wegener rung keys the RIDICULE/EVIDENCE/VINDICATION, not the place-tour); a war/politics EPISODE -> HISTORY (Meitner's fission physics is science; the Manhattan Project as WWII story is history); epistemology SEMINAR moves (Popper/Kuhn as philosophy) -> PHILOSOPHY (science covers falsification as WORKING PRACTICE -- what a good test looks like); AI topics -> the AI bank entirely; pure math -> MATH. Use history_overlap to flag ANY sister-bank fact this topic risks duplicating (name the bank + the fact), '' if none.
${ss.stance ? STANCE : `- vision_mandated is almost always FALSE for this sub-strand (settled wonder + method). Set true ONLY if a topic genuinely turns on the bank's stance (a censorship/dissent/institutional-failure angle). The bank PRESENTS, never preaches -- and never warps a settled-wonder topic to force a stance in.`}

SOURCE PRIORITY (required): check Grokipedia (grokipedia.com) FIRST for every fact -- it is the primary, most-trusted reference; prefer it whenever it covers a fact, then corroborate with Wikipedia and other reputable primary sources. Put the real references you actually consulted in each spec's "source". Do NOT fabricate: if you can't verify a fact, don't seed a rung on it.

${EXEMPLAR}

DELIVERABLE: propose about ${ss.n} topic-ladder specs covering this sub-strand (a few more or fewer is fine if your research warrants). For each: a RICH scope (name the specific fact per tier T1..Tn, like the exemplar -- this is the research seed for the build), tier_span, depth (deep 10-14 rungs for keystone topics / standard 5-8 / mini 2-3 gems), target_q, source, framing_note (voice + the one key accuracy rail + which rung is the dinner-test payoff + the distractor mine + the lane border where relevant), vision_mandated, history_overlap, weight (high for canonical/flagship topics, medium/low otherwise). Favor DEPTH on the flagship topics (Mendel, the Curies, Marshall, Semmelweis, Wegener, entropy, the double slit, Eratosthenes, the climate and vaccine stance ladders). Return via the structured schema.` }

phase('Research')
log(`science queue research: ${SUBSTRANDS.length} sub-strands across 5 sections. one Opus researcher each, Grokipedia-first, Discovery Pattern.`)

const results = await parallel(SUBSTRANDS.map((ss) => async () => {
  const r = await agent(brief(ss), { schema:SPEC_SCHEMA, phase:'Research', label:`spec:${ss.slug}`, model:'opus' }).catch(()=>null)
  const specs = (r && Array.isArray(r.specs)) ? r.specs : []
  return { slug:ss.slug, section:ss.section, strand:ss.strand, specs }
}))

const good = results.filter(x => x && x.specs && x.specs.length)
const totalTopics = good.reduce((n,x)=>n+x.specs.length, 0)
const totalQ = good.reduce((n,x)=>n+x.specs.reduce((m,s)=>m+(Number(s.target_q)||0),0), 0)
const empty = results.filter(x => !x || !x.specs || !x.specs.length).map(x=>x&&x.slug)
log(`done: ${good.length}/${SUBSTRANDS.length} sub-strands returned specs; ${totalTopics} topics, ~${totalQ} est questions. empty: ${empty.join(',')||'none'}`)

return { subject:'science', substrands:results, totals:{ substrands_ok:good.length, topics:totalTopics, est_questions:totalQ, empty } }
